texts:
To factor the expression $ab+5b+2a+10$, we look for common factors and group terms to make factoring easier.

First, we can group the terms as follows:
\begin{align*}
ab + 5b + 2a + 10 &= (ab + 5b) + (2a + 10) \\
\end{align*}

Now, we can factor out the common factors from each group:
\begin{align*}
(ab + 5b) + (2a + 10) &= b(a + 5) + 2(a + 5) \\
\end{align*}

Notice that both terms have a common factor of $(a + 5)$. We can factor this out:
\begin{align*}
b(a + 5) + 2(a + 5) &= (a + 5)(b + 2) \\
\end{align*}

Therefore, the expression $ab+5b+2a+10$ factors into \boxed{(a + 5)(b + 2)}.

